let __v_299 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"london\",\"May, June and September: 18-22C and the long evenings. July and August are warm and crowded, and November to February is grey, wet and dark by 4.30pm.\"],[\"edinburgh\",\"May, June and September: 15-20C, and daylight until nearly 11pm in June; August is the Festival and the Fringe, which is either why you go or when to avoid. November to February is dark by 4pm.\"],[\"bath\",\"May to September for the baths, the crescent and the canal; April and October are quieter and still fine. December is the Christmas market, which is the busiest weekend of the year.\"],[\"dublin\",\"May, June and September: 16-20C and the longest days. July and August are the driest and busiest, and November to February is wet, with dark by 4.30pm.\"],[\"amsterdam\",\"April to June and September: 15-22C and the canals at their best, with the tulips at Keukenhof in late April. July and August are the busiest, and November to February is cold, wet and dark early.\"],[\"brussels\",\"May, June and September: 17-22C, and the Grand Place flower carpet in mid-August every second year. July and August are warm and quiet at weekends, and winter is grey and wet.\"],[\"paris\",\"April to June and September to early October: 18-24C and the parks at their best. July and August are hot and many small restaurants close, and November to February is grey and cool.\"],[\"munich\",\"May to September: 20-25C, beer gardens and the Alps an hour away; late September is Oktoberfest, which doubles hotel prices. December brings the Christmas markets.\"],[\"zurich\",\"May to September for the lake, the old town and the mountain railways, at 22-26C in midsummer. December to February is cold and clear, which is when the Alps look their best.\"],[\"berlin\",\"May to September: 20-25C, outdoor cafes, the lakes, and the city at its most relaxed. July and August are the warmest and busiest, and November to February is grey and cold.\"],[\"prague\",\"April to June and September: 15-22C and the old town before the crush. July and August are busy and 25C+, and December is cold with the Christmas markets.\"],[\"vienna\",\"April to June and September: 18-24C, and the ball season runs January to March. July and August are hot and the opera houses close, and December has the markets.\"],[\"budapest\",\"April to June and September: 20-26C, and the thermal baths are good in cool weather too. July and August are 30C+, and December brings the Christmas markets along the Danube.\"],[\"krakow\",\"May to September: 20-25C and the main square at its best; April and October are quiet and still fine. December to February is cold with snow and a Christmas market.\"],[\"ljubljana\",\"May, June and September: 20-26C, and Lake Bled is warm enough to swim from June. July and August are the busiest, and winter is cold and quiet.\"],[\"copenhagen\",\"May to August: 18-22C, long days, and the harbour baths open from June. July is the busiest and the jazz festival, and November to February is dark by 4pm and cold.\"],[\"stockholm\",\"May to August: 18-23C and light until late, with midsummer at the end of June. The archipelago is best from July to mid-August, and winter is dark with short days.\"],[\"helsinki\",\"June to August: 18-23C with almost no night, and the archipelago ferries running. January and February are the coldest, with the best chance of snow, and December is dark.\"],[\"tallinn\",\"June to August: 18-22C, the old town at its best and white nights in June. December to February is cold and snowy, and the Christmas market is one of the prettiest in Europe.\"],[\"reykjavik\",\"June to August gives midnight sun, open highland roads and puffins; February and March are best for the northern lights. November is dark, wet and icy, so it is the one month I would skip.\"],[\"oslo\",\"May to September: 18-23C, and the fjord islands are a ferry ride from the centre. June has the longest days, and November to February is cold and dark, with skiing an hour out of town.\"],[\"bergen\",\"May to September: 15-19C and the fjord trips running, with light until late in June and July. It rains most of the year, so pack a shell whatever the month.\"],[\"rome\",\"April, May, late September and October: 20-26C and the ruins walkable. July and August are 30C+ with the fountains as the only relief, and August means half the restaurants shut.\"],[\"venice\",\"April, May, late September and October: 18-24C, warm, not crowded and everything open. July and August are hot and packed, and November to January brings acqua alta.\"],[\"florence\",\"April to June and September to October: 20-28C and the galleries without the August crush. July and August are 30C+ and busy, and winter means cool days and short queues.\"],[\"milan\",\"April to June and September: 20-27C and the aperitivo season. July and August are hot and humid and the city half empties, and January is cold with the sales on.\"],[\"naples\",\"April to June and September: 22-27C, with the ferries to Capri and the Amalfi coast running. July and August are hot and busy, and November to March is quiet and wet.\"],[\"lisbon\",\"May, June and September: warm and dry with fewer people. July and August are hot and busy with the tourists, and November to February is wet, though milder than the north.\"],[\"porto\",\"May, June and September: 18-24C and dry, with the Douro valley at its best and the vines in leaf. July and August are warm and busy, and November to March is wet and grey.\"],[\"valencia\",\"April to June and September to October: 20-26C, and the sea still swimmable in October. July and August are 30C+ and busy, and March is Las Fallas if you want the crowds.\"],[\"granada\",\"April to June and September to October: 18-28C, and the Alhambra bookable without a fight. July and August are 35C+ inland, and winter is cold up at the Alhambra.\"],[\"san sebastian\",\"June to September: 20-24C for the beach and the pintxos, with the film festival at the end of September. July and August are the busiest, and the rest of the year is wet.\"],[\"barcelona\",\"May, June and September: 22-27C, the sea warm enough to swim and the terraces full. August is hot and packed, and November to February is cool with some rain.\"],[\"madrid\",\"April, May, June and September: 20-28C and dry, with the terraces out and the Prado quiet. July and August are 35C+ and the city empties, and winter is cold and clear.\"],[\"seville\",\"March to May and October: 20-28C and the orange trees in flower or in fruit, with Semana Santa and the April fair the peak. July and August are 40C+, so people live at night.\"],[\"athens\",\"April, May, October and early November: 20-26C and the sites walkable. July and August are 35C+ and the Acropolis is a scramble by 10am, and the islands are at their best in June and September.\"],[\"santorini\",\"May, June, September and early October: 24-27C, warm sea and no crush. July and August are 30C+ with the cruise crowds landing mid-morning, and many hotels close from November to March.\"],[\"crete\",\"May, June, September and early October: 24-28C and the sea warm, and the Samaria gorge opens in May. July and August are 30C+ and busy, and winter is mild on the south coast.\"],[\"split\",\"May, June, September and early October: 22-27C, with the ferries to Hvar and Brac running. July and August are the peak and the old town is packed by day, and many islands shut from October.\"],[\"dubrovnik\",\"May, June, September and early October: 22-27C and the city walls walkable. July and August are the peak and the cruise ships fill the old town by 10am, and winter is quiet.\"],[\"zadar\",\"May, June and September: 22-27C and the sea warm enough to swim, with the Kornati islands as a day trip. July and August are busy, and winter is quiet.\"],[\"istanbul\",\"April, May, September and October: 18-25C and dry, and the Bosphorus ferries at their best. July and August are hot and humid, and December to February is cold and wet.\"],[\"tokyo\",\"Late March to April for the blossom, and October to November for the autumn colour and the clearest skies. June is the rainy season, August is hot and humid, and the New Year week closes many places.\"],[\"kyoto\",\"Late March to early April for the blossom, and mid-November for the maples. July and August are hot and humid, and the New Year week is the busiest of the year.\"],[\"bangkok\",\"November to February: dry, warm and clear, which is why it is the season. March to May is hot and hazy, and June to October is the monsoon with short, heavy afternoon rain.\"],[\"hanoi\",\"October to December: 20-26C, dry and clear. January to March is cool and damp with drizzle, and May to September is hot and wet, with the heaviest rain in July and August.\"],[\"singapore\",\"Any month works: it is 30C and humid all year, with rain in short bursts. February to April is the driest, November to January the wettest, and the haze can arrive in September.\"],[\"dubai\",\"November to March, when it is 20-30C and you can be outside. From June to September it is over 40C, so people live in air conditioning and the hotel prices fall.\"],[\"marrakech\",\"March to May and October to November: 20-28C by day, cool at night, no extreme heat. July and August are 40C+ in the city, and the desert is cold at night all year.\"],[\"cape town\",\"November to March: dry, 25-28C, the beaches and the Table Mountain cableway at their best. July and August are wet and windy, which is the whale season in Hermanus.\"],[\"havana\",\"November to April: dry and 24-28C. May to October is hot and wet, and August to October is hurricane season, though the rain usually comes in short afternoon storms.\"],[\"buenos aires\",\"March to May and September to November: 18-25C and the parks at their best. December to February is hot and humid and the city empties in January, and July and August are cool and damp.\"],[\"rio de janeiro\",\"December to March is hot, 28-32C, and Carnival falls in February or early March. May to October is cooler and drier, and the sea is still warm in September.\"],[\"mexico city\",\"March to May: dry, warm and clear, before the rains. June to October is the wet season with short afternoon storms, and December to February is dry with cold nights.\"],[\"sydney\",\"September to November and March to May: 20-26C, warm without the scorch. December to February is 30C+ and the beaches are packed, and June to August is mild, with whale watching.\"],[\"melbourne\",\"March to May and September to November: 18-24C, and the city is at its best in autumn. December to February is hot and changeable, and winter is cold and football.\"],[\"delhi\",\"October to March: dry and cooler, 15-25C. April to June is brutally hot at 40C+, and the monsoon runs July to September with flooding in some years.\"],[\"mumbai\",\"November to February: dry, 25-30C and the most comfortable. March to June is hot and humid, and the monsoon runs June to September with heavy rain.\"],[\"new york\",\"May to June and September to October: mild and walkable at 20-26C. July and August are hot and humid, January and February are cold with snow, and the Christmas weeks are the most expensive of the year.\"],[\"boston\",\"May, June, September and October: 18-26C, and October for the foliage. July and August are hot and humid, and January and February are cold with snow.\"],[\"chicago\",\"May, June and September: 20-27C and the lakefront at its best. July and August are hot and humid, and January and February are brutal with the wind off the lake.\"],[\"san francisco\",\"September and October: the warmest, clearest months at 18-24C. July and August are foggy and cool, and the rain comes November to March.\"],[\"los angeles\",\"March to May and September to November: 20-26C and clear. June to August is warm but the marine layer can sit all day at the beaches, and winter is mild with the odd storm.\"],[\"toronto\",\"May to June and September to October: 18-25C. July and August are hot and humid, and December to March is cold with snow.\"]]}")?;
frame.store("CITY_BEST_TIME", __v_299.clone())?;
let __v_300 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"cornwall\",\"May, June and September: 16-20C, the coast path at its best and the lanes still quiet. July and August are the warmest weeks and the busiest by a long way, and October is mild and much emptier, with the Atlantic at its biggest.\"],[\"devon\",\"May, June and September: 16-20C, both coasts open and the beaches half empty. Late July and August are the school-holiday crush on the sand and the roads, and October is still mild if you do not mind a shower.\"],[\"lake district\",\"May, June and September for long clear days at 15-20C; September is the quietest dry-ish month and the fells are at their best. July and August bring the crowds to Windermere and the passes, and November to February is wet, dark and often icy on the tops.\"],[\"norfolk\",\"May to September: the Broads and the north Norfolk coast at 18-22C, and the seal trips running. July and August fill the coastal villages, and October to March is quiet, cheap and cold, with huge skies and good birdwatching.\"],[\"yorkshire\",\"May to September: 16-20C, the Dales and the moors dry and open, and the coast best in June and September. The towns are busy at half term and in August, and the moors are bleak from November to February.\"]]}")?;
frame.store("REGION_BEST_TIME", __v_300.clone())?;
let __v_301 = { let __dict_302 = Value::dict(); let __v_304 = frame.load(rt, "CITY_BEST_TIME")?; if !matches!(__v_304, Value::Dict(_)) { return Err(PyExc::type_error("object is not a mapping")); } pyrt::containers::call_method(&__dict_302, "update", &[__v_304])?; let __v_306 = frame.load(rt, "REGION_BEST_TIME")?; if !matches!(__v_306, Value::Dict(_)) { return Err(PyExc::type_error("object is not a mapping")); } pyrt::containers::call_method(&__dict_302, "update", &[__v_306])?; __dict_302 };
frame.store("WHEN_TO_GO", __v_301.clone())?;
let __v_307 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"iceland\",\"June to August gives midnight sun, open highland roads and puffins; February and March are best for the northern lights. November is dark, wet and icy, so it is the one month I would skip.\"],[\"greece\",\"May, June, September and early October: warm sea, open tavernas and no crush. August is 35C and the islands are packed, and many small hotels close from November to March.\"],[\"spain\",\"April to June and September to October, when it is 20-28C and the coast is quiet. July and August are 35C+ inland and busy on the coast; the north stays green and cooler in summer.\"],[\"italy\",\"April, May, late September and October: warm, not crowded, everything open. July and August are hot and packed, and August in the cities means half the restaurants shut.\"],[\"portugal\",\"May, June and September: warm and dry with fewer people. July and August are hot and busy on the Algarve, and the north is wet from November to February.\"],[\"croatia\",\"June and September: the sea is warm and the coast is not yet rammed. July and August are the peak, and many islands shut down entirely from October.\"],[\"turkey\",\"May, June and September for the coast, and April or October for Istanbul. July and August are hot and crowded, and the coast is quiet and mild in winter.\"],[\"japan\",\"Late March to April for the blossom, or October to November for the autumn colour. June is the rainy season, August is hot and humid, and the New Year week is the busiest travel period of the year.\"],[\"thailand\",\"November to February: dry, warm and clear. March to May is hot and hazy, and June to October is the monsoon, when the islands get rough seas and some boats stop.\"],[\"dubai\",\"November to March, when it is 20-30C and you can be outside. From June to September it is over 40C, so people live in air conditioning and the hotel prices fall.\"],[\"new york\",\"May to June and September to October: mild and walkable. July and August are hot and humid, January and February are cold with snow, and the Christmas weeks are the most expensive of the year.\"],[\"norway\",\"June to August for the fjords, the midnight sun and the coastal ferries. The northern lights need September to March and a clear, dark sky, and much of the mountain roads close in winter.\"],[\"scotland\",\"May to September for the Highlands, the islands and the long evenings. Midges are worst in July and August, and November to February has very short days.\"],[\"morocco\",\"March to May and September to November: warm days, cool nights, no extreme heat. July and August are 40C+ inland, and the desert is cold at night all year.\"],[\"mexico\",\"November to April is the dry season, which is why it is the busy one. May to October is hot and wet, with rain usually in short afternoon storms.\"],[\"australia\",\"September to November and March to May for the south: warm, not scorching. December to February is 35C+ in Sydney and Melbourne, and the north is tropical wet season then.\"],[\"india\",\"October to March for most of the country: dry and cooler. April to June is brutally hot in the north, and the monsoon runs June to September.\"],[\"usa\",\"It depends where: May and September for the northeast, spring and autumn for the southwest, and June to September for the national parks and mountains. Avoid the July 4th week and Thanksgiving for flights.\"]]}")?;
frame.store("BEST_TIME", __v_307.clone())?;
let __v_308 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"fiumicino\",\"the Leonardo Express to Termini is 32 minutes and €14, or a regional train to Trastevere and the metro for less. A taxi is a flat €55 to the centre.\"],[\"lisbon airport\",\"the metro (red line) into town is 20 minutes for about €2 with a Viva card; a taxi is 15-20 minutes and €15-20. Uber works too.\"],[\"charles de gaulle\",\"the RER B into the centre is 35 minutes and about €11.80; a taxi is a flat €56 to the right bank. Orly has the Orlyval plus RER, and a tram now too.\"],[\"barcelona airport\",\"the Aerobus to Plaza Catalunya is 35 minutes and about €7.50; the train to Sants is cheaper and slower. A taxi is a flat €35.\"],[\"amsterdam airport\",\"the train to Centraal is 15-20 minutes and about €6; buy the ticket from the machine before the gates, not on board.\"],[\"dublin airport\",\"the Aircoach or the 747 bus to the centre is about €7-10 and 30-45 minutes; a taxi is €25-30. There is no train link yet.\"],[\"edinburgh airport\",\"the tram or the 100 bus to the centre is about 30 minutes and £6.50; a taxi is £25-30. The tram stops at Haymarket and Princes Street.\"],[\"jfk\",\"the AirTrain plus the subway is about €10 and 60-75 minutes; the LIRR from Jamaica is faster. A yellow cab is a flat fare to Manhattan, plus tolls and tip.\"],[\"berlin airport\",\"the FEX or S9 train to Hauptbahnhof is 30 minutes and about €4.40; a taxi is €40-50.\"],[\"porto airport\",\"the metro line E to the centre is 30 minutes for about €2 with an Andante card; a taxi is 20-25 minutes and €20-25.\"],[\"dubrovnik airport\",\"the Atlas shuttle to the old town is about €8 and 30-40 minutes, timed to the flights; a taxi is €40-50. There is no train.\"],[\"krakow airport\",\"the train to the main station is 20 minutes for about 12 zloty, and bus 252 runs too; a taxi is 25-30 minutes and 70-90 zloty.\"],[\"budapest airport\",\"bus 100E to Deak Ferenc ter is 30 minutes for about 900 forint, and no metro reaches the airport; a taxi is 25-30 minutes and about 10,000 forint.\"],[\"venice airport\",\"the ATVO bus to Piazzale Roma is 20 minutes and €10, and the Alilaguna boat to San Marco is 75 minutes and €15; a water taxi is €100+.\"],[\"copenhagen airport\",\"the metro to Kongens Nytorv is 15 minutes and about 30 kroner, and the train also runs to the central station; a taxi is 250-300 kroner.\"],[\"athens airport\",\"metro line 3 to Syntagma is 40 minutes and €9, and the X95 bus is €5.50 and slower; a taxi is 35-45 minutes and €40.\"],[\"seville airport\",\"the EA airport bus to the centre is 35 minutes and €4; a taxi is 20 minutes and about €25. There is no train link.\"],[\"florence airport\",\"the T2 tram to Santa Maria Novella is 20 minutes and €1.50; a taxi is 20 minutes and about €25.\"],[\"marrakech airport\",\"bus 19 to the medina is 30 minutes and 30 dirham; a taxi should be about 100 dirham, and agree the price before you get in.\"],[\"naples airport\",\"the Alibus to the central station and the port is 20-25 minutes and €5; a taxi is about €25, agreed first.\"],[\"madrid airport\",\"the metro line 8 to Nuevos Ministerios is about €5 and 40 minutes; the Cercanias train to Atocha is faster. A taxi is a flat €33.\"],[\"prague airport\",\"bus 119 to the metro at Nadrazi Veleslavin is 15 minutes and 40 koruna, then the metro, or the Airport Express bus to the main station in about 40 minutes; a taxi is 30 minutes and 500-600 koruna, and agree the price first.\"],[\"istanbul airport\",\"the metro or the Havaist bus to the centre is about €2-5 and takes 40-60 minutes; a taxi is much more and the traffic is bad.\"],[\"lisbon\",\"the metro (red line) into town is 20 minutes for about €2 with a Viva card; a taxi is 15-20 minutes and €15-20.\"],[\"rome\",\"from Fiumicino the Leonardo Express to Termini is 32 minutes and €14; the regional train plus metro is cheaper. A taxi is a flat €55.\"],[\"paris\",\"from Charles de Gaulle the RER B is 35 minutes and about €11.80; from Orly the Orlyval plus RER, or the tram. A taxi from CDG is a flat €56 to the right bank.\"],[\"vienna airport\",\"the S-Bahn S7 to Wien Mitte is 25 minutes for about €4.60, and the City Airport Train is 16 minutes and €14.90. A taxi is a flat €40.\"],[\"zurich airport\",\"the train to the main station is 10 to 12 minutes for about 7 francs, and it runs every few minutes. A taxi is 30 to 40 francs and slower.\"],[\"munich airport\",\"the S-Bahn S1 or S8 to the centre is 40 minutes on a normal city ticket, about €13; a taxi is €70 or more and no quicker in traffic.\"],[\"frankfurt airport\",\"the S-Bahn S8 or S9 to the main station is 15 minutes and about €6.50; a taxi is 25 minutes and €35-40.\"],[\"stockholm airport\",\"the Arlanda Express to the central station is 20 minutes and about 320 kronor, and the commuter train is 40 minutes and cheaper; the express is the most expensive way. A taxi is 45 minutes and 500 kronor or more.\"],[\"oslo airport\",\"the Flytoget to the central station is 20 minutes for about 240 kroner, and the Vy regional train is slower and half the price. A taxi is 45 minutes and very expensive.\"],[\"helsinki airport\",\"the I or P train to the central station is 30 minutes for about €4.10, and it is the same ticket as the city trams.\"],[\"tokyo airport\",\"Haneda is the quick one: the monorail to Hamamatsucho is 20 minutes for about 500 yen, and the Keikyu line goes to Shinagawa. From Narita the Skyliner to Ueno is 41 minutes and about 2,570 yen.\"],[\"kyoto\",\"Kansai airport is 75 minutes away on the Haruka train, which is the easiest way; a taxi is not worth the price.\"],[\"brussels airport\",\"the train to the central station is 20 minutes and about €11, and it runs four times an hour. From Charleroi the bus to Midi takes an hour.\"],[\"bangkok airport\",\"the Airport Rail Link from Suvarnabhumi to Phaya Thai is 30 minutes for 45 baht, and the metro joins it there. A taxi with tolls is 40 to 60 minutes and 400 to 500 baht.\"],[\"singapore airport\",\"the MRT to the city is 30 to 40 minutes for about S$2, changing at Tanah Merah. A taxi is 20 to 30 minutes and S$20-30 with the airport surcharge.\"],[\"hanoi airport\",\"bus 86 to the old quarter is 45 minutes for 35,000 dong, and a Grab or a taxi is about 350,000 dong and 40 minutes.\"],[\"cape town airport\",\"an Uber or a taxi to the centre is 20 to 30 minutes and about 250 rand. There is a train, but not one to take with bags.\"],[\"mexico city airport\",\"the metro line 5 is the cheap way and slow with luggage; a taxi from the official stand inside the terminal is 30 to 45 minutes and about 250 pesos.\"],[\"havana airport\",\"a taxi to the old town is 25 to 30 minutes and about 25 dollars or the same in euros; the airport bus is not worth the wait.\"],[\"buenos aires airport\",\"Ezeiza is 45 minutes by taxi and about 30 dollars, and bus 8 is the cheap way but slow. Aeroparque is in the city itself.\"],[\"rio airport\",\"Galeao is 30 to 50 minutes by taxi, and the BRT bus to the centre is cheaper and takes about an hour. Santos Dumont is in the city.\"],[\"sydney airport\",\"the Airport Link train to Central is 13 minutes for about 20 Australian dollars. A taxi is 25 to 35 dollars and slower in the morning peak.\"],[\"toronto airport\",\"the UP Express to Union station is 25 minutes for about 12 Canadian dollars and runs every 15 minutes.\"],[\"chicago airport\",\"the CTA Blue Line from O'Hare runs all night, 45 minutes for $5. A taxi is 40 to 60 minutes and $50 or more with the tip.\"],[\"boston airport\",\"the Silver Line SL1 bus from the terminals takes about 20 minutes for a normal subway fare, and the water taxi across the harbour is the fun way.\"],[\"san francisco airport\",\"BART to the city is 30 minutes for about $10. A taxi is 25 to 40 minutes and $50 or more.\"],[\"los angeles airport\",\"the FlyAway bus to Union Station is about 45 minutes and $10; a taxi or a rideshare is 30 to 60 minutes and $50 or more, depending on the traffic.\"]]}")?;
frame.store("AIRPORT_TRANSFER", __v_308.clone())?;
let __v_309 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"dubrovnik\",\"Dubrovnik (DBV) is 20km south-east, and the Atlas shuttle to the old town is about €8 and 30-40 minutes, timed to the flights; a taxi is €40-50.\"],[\"krakow\",\"Krakow John Paul II (KRK) is 11km west, and the train to the main station is 20 minutes for about 12 zloty; a taxi is 70-90 zloty.\"],[\"budapest\",\"Budapest Ferenc Liszt (BUD) is 16km south-east, and bus 100E to Deak Ferenc ter is 30 minutes for about 900 forint; a taxi is about 10,000 forint.\"],[\"venice\",\"Venice has two: Marco Polo (VCE) for most flights, 13km north, and Treviso (TSF) for budget ones, 40km away. From Marco Polo the ATVO bus to Piazzale Roma is 20 minutes and €10.\"],[\"athens\",\"Athens (ATH) is 20km east, and metro line 3 to Syntagma is 40 minutes and €9; a taxi is €40.\"],[\"copenhagen\",\"Copenhagen (CPH) is 8km south-east, and the metro to Kongens Nytorv is 15 minutes for about 30 kroner.\"],[\"florence\",\"Florence (FLR) is 5km north-west and small, and the T2 tram to Santa Maria Novella is 20 minutes for €1.50; a taxi is about €25.\"],[\"seville\",\"Seville (SVQ) is 10km north-east, and the EA bus to the centre is 35 minutes for €4; there is no train link.\"],[\"london\",\"London City (LCY) is the closest to the centre: about 25 minutes to Bank on the DLR. London has five, though, and which one suits depends where you are going: Heathrow (LHR) for most long-haul, Gatwick (LGW) for charters and short-haul, City itself if you are staying in the east. From Heathrow the Piccadilly line is an hour and about £5-6.\"],[\"rome\",\"Rome has two: Fiumicino (FCO), the main one, 30km south-west, and Ciampino (CIA) for budget flights, 15km east. From Fiumicino the Leonardo Express is 32 minutes to Termini for €14.\"],[\"lisbon\",\"Lisbon Humberto Delgado (LIS) is 7km north of the centre, and the red metro line takes 20 minutes for about €2 with a Viva card.\"],[\"porto\",\"Porto Francisco Sa Carneiro (OPO) is 11km north-west, and the metro line E to the centre takes about 30 minutes for €2; a taxi is €25-30.\"],[\"paris\",\"Paris has two: Charles de Gaulle (CDG) for most long-haul, 25km north-east, and Orly (ORY) to the south for domestic and short-haul. The RER B from CDG is 35 minutes and about €11.80.\"],[\"barcelona\",\"Barcelona El Prat (BCN) is 12km south-west, and the Aerobus to Plaza Catalunya is 35 minutes and about €7.50.\"],[\"madrid\",\"Madrid-Barajas (MAD) is 12km north-east, and the metro line 8 into the centre is about €5 and 40 minutes; a taxi is a flat €33.\"],[\"amsterdam\",\"Amsterdam Schiphol (AMS) is 15km south-west, and the train to Centraal is 15-20 minutes for about €6.\"],[\"dublin\",\"Dublin (DUB) is 10km north, and the Aircoach or the 747 bus to the centre is about €7-10 and 30-45 minutes; there is no train link yet.\"],[\"edinburgh\",\"Edinburgh (EDI) is 13km west, and the tram or the 100 bus to the centre takes about 30 minutes for £6.50.\"],[\"new york\",\"New York has three: JFK for most international flights, Newark (EWR) for many too, and LaGuardia (LGA) for domestic. From JFK the AirTrain plus the subway is about $10 and 60-75 minutes.\"],[\"berlin\",\"Berlin Brandenburg (BER) is 25km south-east, and the FEX or S9 train to Hauptbahnhof is 30 minutes for about €4.40.\"],[\"prague\",\"Prague Vaclav Havel (PRG) is 15km west, and bus 119 to the metro, or the Airport Express to the main station, is about €1.50-2.50.\"],[\"istanbul\",\"Istanbul has two: IST on the European side, the main one, and SAW on the Asian side for budget flights. From IST the metro or the Havaist bus is 40-60 minutes.\"],[\"milan\",\"For Milan it is Malpensa (MXP) for long-haul, 50km north-west, or Linate (LIN) for short-haul, 7km east. The Malpensa Express to the centre is 50 minutes.\"],[\"dubai\",\"Dubai International (DXB) is 5km from the centre, and the metro red line reaches most of the city for a few dirhams.\"],[\"vienna\",\"Vienna (VIE) is 18km south-east, and the S-Bahn S7 to Wien Mitte is 25 minutes for about €4.60; the City Airport Train is 16 minutes and €14.90. A taxi is a flat €40.\"],[\"stockholm\",\"Stockholm Arlanda (ARN) is 40km north, and the Arlanda Express is 20 minutes and about 320 kronor; the commuter train takes 40 minutes and costs less. Bromma (BMA) is close to the city but only for domestic flights.\"],[\"tokyo\",\"Tokyo has two: Haneda (HND), 20km south and the convenient one, and Narita (NRT), 60km east, which most long-haul flights use. From Haneda the monorail to Hamamatsucho is 20 minutes for about 500 yen.\"],[\"brussels\",\"Brussels (BRU) is 12km north-east, and the train to the central station is 20 minutes for about €11. Charleroi (CRL) is the budget airport, 60km south, and the bus into town takes an hour.\"],[\"munich\",\"Munich (MUC) is 38km north-east, and the S-Bahn S1 or S8 to the centre is 40 minutes for about €13; a taxi is €70 or more.\"],[\"zurich\",\"Zurich (ZRH) is 12km north, and the train to the main station is 10 to 12 minutes for about 7 francs, which is the easiest airport transfer in Europe.\"],[\"oslo\",\"Oslo Gardermoen (OSL) is 47km north, and the Flytoget is 20 minutes for about 240 kroner; the Vy regional train is slower and about half the price.\"],[\"helsinki\",\"Helsinki-Vantaa (HEL) is 20km north, and the I or P train to the central station is 30 minutes for about €4.10.\"],[\"tallinn\",\"Tallinn (TLL) is 4km from the centre, so it is a tram or a short taxi rather than a transfer: tram 4 gets you in for the price of a city ticket.\"],[\"reykjavik\",\"Keflavik (KEF) is the airport people mean, 50km south-west, and the Flybus to the city is 45 minutes for about 3,500 kroner. Reykjavik (RKV) is a small city airport for domestic flights only.\"],[\"boston\",\"Boston Logan (BOS) is 6km east, and the Silver Line SL1 bus from the terminals takes about 20 minutes for a normal subway fare; the water taxi across the harbour is the fun way in.\"],[\"san francisco\",\"San Francisco (SFO) is 21km south, and BART to the city is 30 minutes for about $10. Oakland (OAK) is across the bay and often cheaper.\"],[\"los angeles\",\"Los Angeles (LAX) is 30km south-west and the one people mean; the FlyAway bus to Union Station is about 45 minutes. Hollywood Burbank (BUR) is closer for domestic flights.\"],[\"chicago\",\"Chicago O'Hare (ORD) is 27km north-west, and the CTA Blue Line runs all night, 45 minutes for $5. Midway (MDW) is nearer the city and on the Orange Line.\"],[\"toronto\",\"Toronto Pearson (YYZ) is 27km north-west, and the UP Express to Union station is 25 minutes for about 12 Canadian dollars.\"],[\"sydney\",\"Sydney (SYD) is 8km south, and the Airport Link train to Central is 13 minutes for about 20 Australian dollars; a taxi is 25 to 35.\"],[\"singapore\",\"Singapore Changi (SIN) is 20km east, and the MRT to the city is 30 to 40 minutes for about S$2. Allow an hour there before your flight: the Jewel waterfall is inside the airport.\"],[\"bangkok\",\"Bangkok has two: Suvarnabhumi (BKK), the main one 30km east, and Don Mueang (DMK), 25km north, for budget flights. From Suvarnabhumi the Airport Rail Link is 30 minutes for 45 baht.\"],[\"hanoi\",\"Hanoi (HAN) is 35km north, and bus 86 to the old quarter is 45 minutes for 35,000 dong; a taxi or a Grab is about 350,000 dong and 40 minutes.\"],[\"cape town\",\"Cape Town (CPT) is 20km east, and a taxi or an Uber to the centre is 20 to 30 minutes and about 250 rand. There is a train, but not one to take with bags.\"],[\"mexico city\",\"Mexico City (MEX) is 13km east, and the metro line 5 is cheap and slow; a taxi from the official stand inside the terminal is 30 to 45 minutes and about 250 pesos.\"],[\"havana\",\"Havana (HAV) is 15km south of the city, and a taxi to the old town is 25 to 30 minutes and about 25 dollars or the same in euros; the airport bus is not worth the wait.\"],[\"buenos aires\",\"Buenos Aires has two: Ezeiza (EZE), 30km south, for long-haul, and Aeroparque (AEP) in the city for domestic flights. From Ezeiza a taxi is 45 minutes and about 30 dollars; bus 8 is the cheap way.\"],[\"rio de janeiro\",\"Rio has two: Galeao (GIG), 20km north, for international flights, and Santos Dumont (SDU) in the city for the Sao Paulo shuttle. From Galeao a taxi is 30 to 50 minutes.\"],[\"naples\",\"Naples (NAP) is 6km north-east, and the Alibus to the central station and the port is 20 minutes for €5; a taxi is about €25, and agree the price first.\"],[\"valencia\",\"Valencia (VLC) is 9km west, and metro line 3 or 5 to the centre is 20 minutes for about €5.\"],[\"granada\",\"Granada (GRX) is 17km west and small, and the airport bus to the centre is 40 minutes for €3. Most people fly to Malaga instead and take the bus, which is two hours.\"],[\"santorini\",\"Santorini (JTR) is 6km from Fira, and the bus meets the flights; a taxi is 20 to 30 euros. It is a small airport with a short runway, so summer flights are often delayed.\"],[\"san sebastian\",\"San Sebastian (EAS) is 20km east at Hondarribia and has very few flights, so most people fly to Bilbao (75 minutes by bus) or Biarritz (40 minutes).\"],[\"ljubljana\",\"Ljubljana (LJU) is 25km north, and the airport bus to the centre is 30 minutes for about €4; a taxi is €25 to €30.\"],[\"kyoto\",\"Kyoto has no airport of its own: fly into Osaka Kansai (KIX), which is 75 minutes away on the Haruka train, or into Tokyo and take the shinkansen.\"],[\"bath\",\"Bath has no airport: Bristol (BRS) is 30km west, and the Flyer bus runs to Bath in 55 minutes. By train, come into Bath Spa from Bristol Temple Meads.\"]]}")?;
frame.store("AIRPORT_NAME", __v_309.clone())?;
let __v_310 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"london\",\"Bath (80 minutes by train), Oxford and Cambridge (about an hour), and Brighton (an hour) for the sea. Book the train a week ahead and you halve the fare.\"],[\"edinburgh\",\"Glasgow (50 minutes by train from Waverley), Stirling for the castle (50 minutes), and North Berwick (35 minutes) for the beach and the boat out to the Bass Rock. St Andrews is about 90 minutes by train and bus, and worth the day for the ruins and the beach rather than the golf.\"],[\"paris\",\"Versailles (40 minutes on the RER C), Chartres for the cathedral, and Giverny for Monet's garden from April to October. Go early: the first trains are the quietest.\"],[\"rome\",\"Ostia Antica for the Roman ruins (30 minutes on the metro and train), Tivoli for the villa gardens, and Orvieto for the cathedral. Pompeii is two hours each way, so it is a full day.\"],[\"lisbon\",\"Sintra for the palaces (40 minutes by train), Cascais for the beach (40 minutes on the same line), and Obidos for the walled town (an hour by bus from Lisbon's Campo Grande, and no train goes there). Buy the train ticket at the machine and go before 9am.\"],[\"barcelona\",\"Montserrat (an hour by train and cable car), Girona (40 minutes) and Sitges for the beach (40 minutes). Girona plus Figures makes a good full day.\"],[\"amsterdam\",\"Haarlem (15 minutes), Utrecht (25 minutes) and the Zaanse Schans windmills (40 minutes). Keukenhof is worth it only in tulip season, mid-March to mid-May.\"],[\"madrid\",\"Toledo (30 minutes by train), Segovia (30 minutes) and El Escorial. Toledo and Segovia both deserve a full day rather than an afternoon.\"],[\"munich\",\"Neuschwanstein (two hours by train and bus), Salzburg (90 minutes) and the Bavarian lakes. Buy a Bayern ticket: it covers the regional trains for a group.\"],[\"edinburgh\",\"Glasgow (50 minutes by train), Stirling for the castle, and North Berwick for the beach and the seabird centre. The Highlands need a car or a full day tour.\"],[\"dublin\",\"Howth for the cliff walk (30 minutes on the DART), Malahide castle, and Glendalough in the Wicklow mountains, which needs a car or a bus tour.\"],[\"berlin\",\"Potsdam for Sanssouci (30 minutes by train) and Sachsenhausen, which is a heavy half-day and worth it. Both are covered by the Berlin ABC travel card.\"],[\"tokyo\",\"Nikko for the shrines and Kamakura for the Buddha (both about two hours), or Hakone for a view of Fuji if the sky is clear. Go on a weekday: the weekend trains are packed.\"],[\"leeds\",\"York (25 minutes by train), the Yorkshire Dales (an hour by car) and Harrogate for a spa afternoon. Manchester is 50 minutes by train if you want a city.\"],[\"florence\",\"Pisa (an hour by train) for the tower, Siena (90 minutes) for the square, and Lucca for the walls and the bikes. Fiesole is 30 minutes by bus for the view back over Florence.\"],[\"venice\",\"Verona (an hour by train) for the arena, Padua for the Scrovegni chapel, and the islands in the lagoon: Murano for glass and Burano for the coloured houses, on a vaporetto day pass.\"],[\"naples\",\"Pompeii and Herculaneum (40 minutes on the Circumvesuviana), the Amalfi coast by ferry or bus, and Ischia for a slower island day. Vesuvius is a bus and a walk from Ercolano.\"],[\"seville\",\"Cordoba for the mosque-cathedral (45 minutes by train), Ronda for the gorge and the bridge, and Jerez for the sherry bodegas. Granada is three hours by bus, so it wants a night.\"],[\"porto\",\"The Douro valley by train to Pinhao for the vineyards, Braga and Guimaraes for the churches and the old town, and Aveiro for the canals. The Douro line is the scenic one, so sit on the right.\"],[\"athens\",\"Cape Sounion for the temple at sunset, Delphi for the ruins (two and a half hours by bus), and Aegina or Hydra by ferry for an island day. The fast ferries are worth the extra.\"],[\"istanbul\",\"The Princes' Islands by ferry (an hour and a half) where there are no cars, Bursa for the Ottoman tombs, and the Bosphorus village of Anadolu Kavagi at the mouth of the Black Sea.\"],[\"prague\",\"Kutna Hora for the bone church and the silver mines (an hour by train), Karlstejn for the castle, and Cesky Krumlov, which is three hours each way so it wants a night.\"],[\"vienna\",\"Bratislava (an hour by train), the Wachau valley by boat for the vineyards and Durnstein, and Baden for the spa. The Einfach-Raus ticket covers a group on the regional trains.\"],[\"brussels\",\"Bruges (an hour by train) for the canals, Ghent (35 minutes) for the old port, and Leuven for the university town. Book Bruges ahead in summer, it fills up.\"],[\"copenhagen\",\"Roskilde for the cathedral and the Viking ships (25 minutes), Malmo across the bridge (35 minutes) for a cheaper lunch, and the Louisiana museum up the coast, which is the best half-day of the lot.\"],[\"stockholm\",\"The archipelago by ferry from Stromkajen, Uppsala for the cathedral and the Vikings (40 minutes by train), and Drottningholm by boat for the palace theatre.\"],[\"split\",\"Hvar by catamaran (an hour) for the old town and the lavender, Trogir (30 minutes by bus) for the walled centre, and Krka for the waterfalls, which needs a car or a tour.\"],[\"dubrovnik\",\"Mostar in Bosnia (two and a half hours by bus) for the bridge, Montenegro for Kotor and the bay, and the Elaphiti islands by boat. Take your passport for Mostar and Montenegro.\"],[\"ljubljana\",\"Lake Bled (an hour by bus) for the island church, Postojna for the caves and the castle, and Skocjan for the bigger cave, which is the one to pick if you only do one.\"],[\"bath\",\"Stonehenge (an hour by bus) with a booked slot, Lacock for the village and the abbey, and Bradford-on-Avon for the canal and the tithe barn, 15 minutes by train.\"],[\"marrakech\",\"The Atlas mountains and Ourika valley (an hour by car), Essaouira for the seafront and the fish (two and a half hours by bus), and Ait Benhaddou, which is a long day or a night on the way to the desert.\"],[\"bangkok\",\"Ayutthaya for the ruined temples (an hour and a half by train), Kanchanaburi for the bridge over the River Kwai, and the floating market at Damnoen Saduak, which needs a very early start.\"],[\"hanoi\",\"Halong Bay for the boats (two and a half hours by bus, and a night on the water is better than a day), Ninh Binh for the river rowing boats, and Sapa by night train for the rice terraces.\"],[\"bristol\",\"Bath (15 minutes by train), Wells for the cathedral, and the Mendips or the Gower if you have a car. Cardiff is 50 minutes by train.\"],[\"manchester\",\"the Peak District (40 minutes by train to Edale), Liverpool (50 minutes) and Chester for the walls and the rows. York is 90 minutes.\"],[\"glasgow\",\"Loch Lomond (40 minutes by train), Stirling for the castle, and Edinburgh in an hour. The islands need a ferry and a full day.\"],[\"liverpool\",\"Chester (40 minutes by train), the Wirral coast, and Manchester in under an hour. North Wales is a longer day by train.\"],[\"birmingham\",\"Stratford-upon-Avon (40 minutes by train), Warwick castle and the Cotswolds by car. The Black Country museum is a good wet-day half-day.\"],[\"new york\",\"Beacon for Dia:Beacon (80 minutes on Metro-North), Philadelphia (90 minutes on Amtrak) and the Hamptons by the LIRR. The Jersey shore is a longer day.\"],[\"chicago\",\"Milwaukee (90 minutes on Amtrak), the Indiana Dunes for the beach (an hour by train and bus) and the Baha'i temple at Wilmette, which is free and half a day on the Purple line.\"],[\"san francisco\",\"Muir Woods and Sausalito (ferry, then a shuttle you book ahead), Napa by car, and Santa Cruz over the hill. Yosemite is four hours, so it wants a night.\"],[\"los angeles\",\"Santa Monica and Malibu down the coast, Disneyland in Anaheim (an hour by car) and Catalina island by ferry from Long Beach. Almost all of it needs a car.\"],[\"boston\",\"Salem for the witch museum (30 minutes by train), Concord and Lexington for the revolution, and Providence (an hour on Amtrak). Cape Cod is 90 minutes by car.\"],[\"toronto\",\"Niagara Falls (two hours by train or bus, and the falls are free), Niagara-on-the-Lake for the wineries on the same trip, and Stratford for the Shakespeare festival.\"],[\"sydney\",\"The Blue Mountains (two hours by train), the Hunter Valley for wine (three hours, better on a tour) and Manly or Watsons Bay by ferry for a beach day close in.\"],[\"singapore\",\"Johor Bahru across the causeway (the bus queue is long at weekends), Batam by ferry, and Malacca, which is three and a half hours each way. The Botanic Gardens and the southern ridges are free and in the city.\"],[\"dubai\",\"Abu Dhabi for the grand mosque and the Louvre (90 minutes by car or bus), the desert for a dune drive, and Hatta for the mountains and the kayaks. The Abu Dhabi bus leaves from Al Ghubaiba.\"],[\"cape town\",\"The Cape of Good Hope and the Boulders Beach penguins, which is a full day by car, Stellenbosch and Franschhoek for wine (an hour), and Hermanus for whales from June to November.\"],[\"mexico city\",\"Teotihuacan for the pyramids (an hour by bus from the north terminal), Puebla and Cholula (two hours by bus), and Taxco for silver, which is a long day.\"],[\"havana\",\"Vinales for the tobacco valley (three hours by bus, better with a night), the beach at Santa Maria del Mar (30 minutes by taxi), and Matanzas for the river and the poets.\"],[\"buenos aires\",\"Tigre for the delta boats (an hour by train), Colonia in Uruguay by ferry (an hour, and take your passport), and San Antonio de Areco for the gaucho town.\"],[\"rio de janeiro\",\"Petropolis for the imperial palace (90 minutes by bus), Niteroi for the museum and the beaches across the bay, and Buzios, which is three hours and wants a night.\"],[\"budapest\",\"Szentendre for the artist town and the Danube bend (40 minutes on the H5 train), Esztergom for the basilica, and Lake Balaton, which is two hours and wants a night.\"],[\"krakow\",\"Auschwitz-Birkenau (90 minutes by bus, and book a timed entry), the Wieliczka salt mine (30 minutes by train) and Zakopane for the mountains (two hours). Auschwitz is a heavy half-day, not a sight.\"],[\"milan\",\"Lake Como for Bellagio (an hour by train to Como, then a boat), Bergamo for the old town (50 minutes) and Turin (an hour on the fast train). The Last Supper needs booking weeks ahead.\"],[\"zurich\",\"Lucerne (45 minutes by train), the Rhine Falls (an hour) and Interlaken for the mountains (two hours). A travel pass covers the trains and the boats.\"],[\"oslo\",\"The fjord by boat from the city hall pier, Drobak for the fortress and the old town (an hour by bus), and Bergen by train, which is the best rail journey in the country and wants a night.\"],[\"helsinki\",\"Suomenlinna by ferry (15 minutes on the same ticket as the trams), Porvoo for the wooden old town (an hour by bus) and Tallinn by ferry (two hours, and take your passport).\"],[\"tallinn\",\"Lahemaa national park for the manors and the coast (an hour by bus), Tartu (two and a half hours) and Helsinki by ferry in two hours.\"],[\"reykjavik\",\"The Golden Circle - Thingvellir, Geysir and Gullfoss - is the full day out and needs a car or a tour, the Blue Lagoon is 45 minutes by bus and booked ahead, and Snaefellsnes is a very long day.\"],[\"santorini\",\"Oia for the sunset and Akrotiri for the Minoan town under the ash are the day, and both are 20 to 30 minutes by bus from Fira; boats to Thirasia and the volcano leave from the old port.\"],[\"valencia\",\"The Albufera for the rice fields and the lagoon (30 minutes by bus), Sagunto for the Roman theatre, and Requena for the wine. The City of Arts is in the city, not a day out.\"],[\"granada\",\"The Alhambra is the day, not a detour: book a timed ticket weeks ahead. The Alpujarras villages are an hour and a half by bus, and Cordoba is two and a half hours by train, so it wants a night.\"],[\"san sebastian\",\"Bilbao for the Guggenheim (an hour and a quarter by bus), Saint-Jean-de-Luz across the French border (40 minutes) and Getaria for the txakoli wine. Hondarribia is 25 minutes by bus.\"],[\"kyoto\",\"Nara for the deer and the great Buddha (45 minutes by train), Osaka (30 minutes) and Hikone for the castle on Lake Biwa. Fushimi Inari and Arashiyama are in Kyoto, so go at dawn instead.\"]]}")?;
