let __v_1237 = Value::from("Check the airport's own website before you fly, on its 'to and from the airport' page: it lists the official ways into the centre with the price and the running time, which saves guessing at a machine after a flight. In most cities the train or metro is the quickest and cheapest way in, so follow the signs for trains or rail rather than the taxi rank; the airport bus or shuttle is cheaper and slower, and a taxi is the most expensive and the easiest with luggage or after dark. Buy the ticket before you board, and ignore anyone inside the terminal offering a taxi.");
frame.store("_AIRPORT_WAY_IN", __v_1237.clone())?;
let __v_1238 = Value::from("The cheapest way in is nearly always the train, the metro or the airport bus, and which of the three depends on the airport: its own 'to and from' page lists every option with the price, and it is worth a look before you fly. If the train or metro goes near where you are staying, take it; if not, take the bus to the main station and carry on from there. A taxi is the last choice for the money, and the most expensive thing you can do is accept a lift from someone who approaches you inside the terminal.");
frame.store("_AIRPORT_CHEAPEST_REPLY", __v_1238.clone())?;
let __v_1239 = Value::from("Fastest is the train or metro where there is one, because a taxi sits in the same traffic as everyone else: an airport express train, where a city has one, is quickest of all for a few euros more, and the metro is close behind. Take a taxi only if you land late, have heavy bags, or the railway does not run at that hour - and then the official rank or a car booked on an app, not anyone offering you a ride indoors.");
frame.store("_AIRPORT_FASTEST_REPLY", __v_1239.clone())?;
let __v_1240 = Value::from("Most big airports have a train or metro into the centre, and the airport's own website says so under 'to and from the airport', with the platform, the price and the last train of the night - check that last one before you book a late flight. Where there is a station sign, follow it: it is almost always cheaper than a taxi, and the ride is usually 15 to 40 minutes. Smaller airports run a bus to the nearest station instead, and a few have no rail link at all, in which case the shuttle bus or the official taxi rank is the way in.");
frame.store("_AIRPORT_TRAIN_REPLY", __v_1240.clone())?;
let __v_1241 = Value::from("Use the hotel's own directions, because they name the station or stop nearest the door and hotels write that down better than anyone: an email to them gets you the answer before you fly. Then take the train or bus into the centre and walk from the station, or hop in a short taxi from there if it is far. A taxi all the way from the airport is the easiest with luggage, so check the price first and take it from the official rank.");
frame.store("_AIRPORT_HOTEL_REPLY", __v_1241.clone())?;
let __v_1242 = Value::from("A cruise port is usually some way from the airport, and the simple answer is the transfer the cruise line sells: it is priced per person and it waits for the plane if the flight is late, which no taxi will. If you would rather make your own way, the port's own website lists the terminal and the local buses, and a taxi is worth it if there are two or more of you with luggage - agree the price before you get in, because port taxis know you have a ship to catch.");
frame.store("_AIRPORT_PORT_REPLY", __v_1242.clone())?;
let __v_1243 = Value::from("Sort the journey the night before rather than on the morning: at 5am the first train often has not started, so it is a taxi booked in advance, a lift, or a hotel at the airport, and an airport hotel is worth its price for a flight before about 7am. Work backwards from the departure time - be there two hours before a short-haul flight and three before a long-haul one, add the journey, and let the drive take 30 minutes more than the map says at that hour. Check the night rate and any drop-off charge when you book, because both cost more at that time.");
frame.store("_AIRPORT_EARLY_REPLY", __v_1243.clone())?;
let __v_1244 = Value::from("It is allowed in most airports and nobody minds, but be ready for it: the seats before security are the bright, busy ones, and the quiet corners are past security, which you cannot reach until check-in opens. For a layover over four hours a pod or an airport hotel is worth the money, and for a short one a hoodie or a scarf as a pillow, an eye mask, and something to drink gets you a couple of hours. Keep your bag looped round an arm, set two alarms, and find out where your gate is before you settle.");
frame.store("_AIRPORT_SLEEP_REPLY", __v_1244.clone())?;
